ujc|a|Well-born; of a good family or respectable birth, though not noble. ; Quiet and refined in manners; not rough, harsh, or stern; mild; meek; bland; amiable; tender; as, a gentle nature, temper, or disposition; a gentle manner; a gentle address; a gentle voice. ; A compellative of respect, consideration, or conciliation; as, gentle reader. ; Not wild, turbulent, or refractory; quiet and docile; tame; peaceable; as, a gentle horse. ; Soft; not violent or rough; not strong, loud, or disturbing; easy; soothing; pacific; as, a gentle touch; a gentle gallop .	j:1le1,72,3~1le1,72,3	e:1awf,29,2~1awf,29,2
uk3|a|Belonging to, or proceeding from, the original stock; native; hence, not counterfeit, spurious, false, or adulterated; authentic; real; natural; true; pure; as, a genuine text; a genuine production; genuine materials.	j:32c,98,4~32c,98,4
